sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Customer Website
    participant API as Node.js API
    participant DB as Supabase PostgreSQL
    participant P as Payment Provider
    participant N as Notification Worker

    C->>API: POST /bookings/draft
    API->>API: Recalculate fare and booking advance
    API->>DB: Create pending_payment booking and fare snapshot
    DB-->>API: ticketId, booking token, amount
    API-->>C: Booking token and advance amount

    C->>API: POST /payments/create-checkout(provider, currency)
    API->>DB: Read persisted amount and create pending payment record
    API->>P: Create checkout/session for exact amount
    P-->>API: Checkout URL or public client token
    API-->>C: Checkout URL or public client token

    C->>P: Complete Razorpay, PayPal, or card checkout
    P->>API: Signed webhook or provider event
    API->>API: Verify signature or server-side payment state
    API->>DB: Compare booking, amount, currency, provider IDs
    alt Valid and not previously processed
        DB->>DB: Mark payment captured and booking paid_confirmed
        DB-->>API: Commit transaction
        API->>N: Queue confirmation notification
        API-->>P: Acknowledge event
    else Duplicate, mismatch, or invalid event
        API->>DB: Record safe rejection or duplicate result
        API-->>P: Acknowledge without paid transition
    end

    C->>API: GET /bookings/:ticketId
    API->>DB: Read authoritative booking state
    DB-->>API: pending_payment or paid_confirmed
    API-->>C: Current verified booking state

    Note over API,DB: Browser redirects and payment callbacks never prove payment.
    Note over P,API: Each provider uses its own signed event or server verification method.
